            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>On account of the merits of Claudia Hedone and the memory of Tiberius Claudius Himerus, her son. The worshippers of Hercules, altogether, having sworn by Jupiter the Best and Greatest
                   and by the genius of Imperator Caesar Nerva Trajan Augustus Germanicus, decreed as follows:
                   they resolved, for themselves and for their descendants, that every year in perpetuity on the sixth day before the Ides of Feburary, they should celebrate the birthday of Tiberius Claudius Himerus
                   and hold a banquet in the temple of Hercules; however, if they should not do so, then in whatever year this obligation has been neglected, these worshippers of Hercules whose [names] have been written
                   on the marble inscription and their descendants, should pay to the worshipeprs of the images of our Caesar, who are in vicus Strament(---), annually, 200 sesterces. MAT(?) (---).
                </p>
